---
import BaseHead from "../components/BaseHead.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from "../consts";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import hyperstar from "../assets/images/hyperstar.jpeg";
import ineq_ss from "../assets/images/ineq-main-menu.png";
import pingfox_ss from "../assets/images/pingfox-static-home.jpeg";
import gotta_lock_in from "../assets/images/Gotta_Lock_In.jpg";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<h1>Sup my homie ;&rpar;</h1>
		<Image
			src="https://github.com/4d1ty.png"
			alt="sup dude, here is my pfp"
			width="100"
			height="100"
			loading="lazy"
			decoding="async"
			id="pfp"
		/>
		<script>
			const pfp = document.querySelector("#pfp");
			if (pfp !== null) {
				let chad = new Audio("chad.mp3");
				pfp.addEventListener("click", () => {
					if (chad.paused) {
						chad.play();
					} else {
						chad.pause();
					}
				});
			}
		</script>
		<p>
			I don't want to say much.
			<br />
			I am a programmer, software developer, whatever you want to call.
			<br />
			Name: <strong>Aditya Priyadarshi</strong> (please don't say my name if
			you can't pronounce it.)
			<br />
			Programming Languages that I know:
			<code>
				<pre>
- Python
- C
- C++
- Java (A little)
- HTML (I know its not a Programming Languages, its a markup language)
- css (I mean after HTML comes css, not much but still)
- Javascript (Yeah, I hate this language, but still I know as you know web)
- SQL (Do you say it as S-Q-L or Sequel?)
- Some Godot Game Dev Programming (Its more like Python) 
- Some RISC Assembly (I did some tinkering with ATTiny85, it was fun)</pre>
			</code>

			<cite
				>Currently suffering the god's wrath. I currently is very sick
				and I might be slow to respond.</cite
			>
		</p>
		<p>
			Also, I am <strong>not a frontend developer</strong>, I repeat I am <strong
				>not a frontend developer</strong
			>
		</p>
		<h4>Some projects:</h4>
		<ol>
			<li>
				<a href="https://github.com/ms1246/Vitary"
					><code>Vitary</code></a
				>
				: Eh, It's a social media webapp which I made few years ago in django.
				It was pretty fun, I even hosted it on pythonanywhere, but the storage
				got over and I had to take it down.
			</li>
			<li>
				<a href="https://github.com/ms1246/PingVille"
					><code>PingVille:</code></a
				>
				<ul>
					<li>
						<a href="https://github.com/foxy4096/pingville-game"
							><code>pingville-game</code></a
						>
						: It's a multiplayer game which I wrote in godot, It's kinda
						like club penguin, I implemented the user accounts and auth
						via the backend vanilla php (yup 💀)
					</li>
					<li>
						<a href="https://github.com/foxy4096/pingville-web"
							><code>pingville-web</code></a
						>
						: This is the actual backend php server which I wrote for
						the <code>pingville-game</code>. Somethings are messy. I
						could had used jwt so as no need to hit the db again and
						again, but what can I say, I might be kinda of stupid 💀
					</li>
				</ul>
			</li>
			<li>
				<a href="https://github.com/ms1246/Nimbus"
					><code>Nimbus</code></a
				>: Not much to say, pretty new project, It's used my esp32
				weather station and collect the data that gets piped in to a api
				route and is stored in a
				<code>weather_data.csv</code>. Currently I am just doing the
				data analysis with pandas and matplotlib, might add some scikit
				learn ml later :&rpar;
